# Environment

Knex version: 3.1.0 (also reproducible on current `master`)
Database + version: sqlite3 (npm package; no live DB connection required to reproduce)
OS: any

# Bug

## 1. Behaviour

Knex supports supplying `connection` as a function (see [configuration docs](https://knexjs.org/guide/#configuration-options)). When using this with the `sqlite3` client, Knex emits a spurious warning at startup:

```
Could not find `connection.filename` in config. Please specify the database path and name to avoid errors. (see docs https://knexjs.org/guide/#configuration-options)
```

This warning was added in #5216 to help catch missing or misspelled `filename` values. However, the check in `lib/dialects/sqlite3/index.js` runs in the constructor against `config.connection` directly:

```js
if (config.connection && config.connection.filename === undefined) {
  this.logger.warn(/* ... */);
}
```

When `connection` is a function, `config.connection.filename` is always `undefined`, even though the resolved connection object (returned by the function on first pool use) will include a valid `filename`. The warning is a false positive.

Expected: no `connection.filename` warning when `connection` is a function.
Actual: warning is logged every time Knex is initialized with a sqlite3 connection function.

## 2. Warning message

```
Could not find `connection.filename` in config. Please specify the database path and name to avoid errors. (see docs https://knexjs.org/guide/#configuration-options)
```

## 3. Reduced test code

No database setup is required — the warning is emitted during client construction, before any query runs.

```js
const knex = require('knex')({
  client: 'sqlite3',
  connection: () => ({
    filename: ':memory:',
  }),
  useNullAsDefault: true,
});

// Observe warning on stderr during construction above.

knex.destroy();
```

Async connection functions are also affected:

```js
const knex = require('knex')({
  client: 'sqlite3',
  connection: async () => ({
    filename: ':memory:',
  }),
  useNullAsDefault: true,
});

knex.destroy();
```

## Related

- #5216 — added the filename warning (closed; shipped in 2.2.0)
- #6136 — proposed fix: skip the warning when `typeof config.connection === 'function'`

