# Environment

Knex version: 3.1.0
Database + version: Oracle 23ai (but all oracles)
OS: Pop_Os

@atiertant - Tagging as this is an oracle feature request

# Feature discussion / request

1. I was excited to use knex to manage in-time migrations for OracleDB across my team.  When I was prototyping this, I ran into the unfortunate circumstance that some of my operations (like adding custom types), required me to perform those under the the SYSDBA role.  After looking at the code for the oracledb client [here](https://github.com/knex/knex/blob/176151d8048b2a7feeb89a3d649a5580786d4f4e/lib/dialects/oracledb/index.js#L129-L164), it looks like there is no way to add the [privilege option for the underlying library](https://node-oracledb.readthedocs.io/en/latest/user_guide/connection_handling.html#privileged-connections).

I came from sequelize usage, where Sequelize has a dialectOptions field to allow for users to configure their driver specific needs and accidentally assumed this was the same case here.  For the current use case, at the very least having either a "privilege" field for oracledb dialect or a dialectOptions field that spreads into the rest of the options would be ideal.

3. Explain what kind of feature would support this

As stated above, some sort of config field that would allow us to configure the driver specific connection options feels like the simplest fix.  If we wanted to minimize it, it could just be for oracleOptions.

```typescript
export default {
  // This would be config for all drivers and would be a little extra scope beyond oracle
  generalForAllConfig: {
    client: 'oracledb',
    connection: {
      user: 'myUser',
      password: '****',
      database: 'DB',
      driverOptions: {
         privilege: oracledb.SYSDBA,
      }
    }
  },
  // This would be a smaller scope with a busier set of fields were this to expand
  justForOracleDbConfig: {
     client: 'oracledb',
    connection: {
      user: 'myUser',
      password: '****',
      database: 'DB',
      oracleOptions: {
         privilege: oracledb.SYSDBA,
      }
    }
  }
}
```

5. Give some API proposal, how the feature should work

From the above defined config, we could roll out driverOptions as a whole config field that will `Supply the provided driver
options to underlying driver that you chose when specifying your client`.  Additionally, I would propose that we overlay the common config items that are explicit on top of the supplied driverOptions to ensure backwards compatibility (i.e. we use the knex common config API first before using this option). 

If we wanted to roll out oracle first as a test case for this, we could throw errors if the client does not yet implement "driverOptions".

Additionally, depending on the knex team's design paradigm, we could also throw errors for any driverOptions that overlap with config keys that knew would normally fill in.  However, that would add additional burden to long term development and may be
better fixed by having documentation say that and letting the user find that out.

## I would be willing to contribute this feature if the knex team agrees on the implementation. 

This feature is blocking my full usage of the knex project to manage migrations so I would be invested in getting a pull request up quickly if we can define the configuration API definitions and error handling that the team agrees on.

Thanks for your time and let me know!

